;; agent$workflow (RFC-076): /workflow. Keeps this project's workflows — the
;; named graphs of stages .brainyard/deps.edn holds under :workflows
;; (RFC-075) — and runs one on a piece of work.
;;
;; Its loop is brainyard/loops/workflow.edn: a request to run a workflow
;; takes each stage through a ReAct turn of its own, judged by the
;; workflow's master role; any other request is one ReAct turn over the
;; workflow$* commands its :config turns on, each change shown to the person
;; and written only on their yes. Every turn has every tool the session has,
;; under the same permission gate and the profile's holds on it; not itself.
{:description
 "Keeps and runs this project's workflows (.brainyard/deps.edn's :workflows: named graphs of stages, each stage playing a role, each link saying what one stage hands the next, a master role supervising a run). Lists them, shows one, and adds, changes or removes one as the person asks — every change shown to them and written only on their yes. Runs one on a piece of work (words, a bead or a GitHub issue): each stage worked in a turn of its own with its role's brief, what it hands on checked, the master judging each handoff, under the project's profile; ends with each stage's outcome. Lists past runs and keeps the person's verdict on one; goes on with a run that waits to be handed on or stopped with a stage left, runs an ended one again told what to change, and runs one on a branch to build on or by hand, waiting after each stage. A run takes minutes to hours."

 :instruction-resource "brainyard/prompts/agents/workflow.md"

 :loop "brainyard/loops/workflow.edn"

 ;; every tool the session has, for a stage's work; but not itself
 :deny-tools ["agent$workflow"]

 ;; it asks the person as it works, so its call is waited on, never detached
 :attended? true

 :tier :standard

 :config {:workflow-tools? true}}
